=== https://help.respondent.io/en/articles/5456426-how-respondent-works-and-how-to-earn-money ===
What&#x27;s Respondent? Respondent is a marketplace that connects researchers with people who want to join paid research studies . You apply with a short screener, researchers choose who to invite , you complete the session (remote or in-person), and then you receive your incentive. How to start earning on Respondent (step-by-step): Browse paid research projects that match your background and interests. Complete a screener (unpaid) to check your fit. If you’re a match, the researcher invites you to participate and (for interviews) book a time . Join the session (either remote or in-person) and complete any assigned tasks. The researcher marks you Attended/Completed → your payment is sent via Tremendous → you redeem the incentive. Key concepts Screener (unpaid): quick questionnaire to verify you match the study. Invite: the researcher’s confirmation that you’ve been selected (often includes a scheduling link). Payment status: in your dashboard, you’ll see Payment Sent (issued) → Paid (successfully delivered via Tremendous). Related Support Articles Project status &amp; invites What is the Status of My Project? I’ve Been Invited to Participate, Now What? Payments What is the Status of My Incentive Payment? Where can I find my project incentive payments? Payment options for Participants Getting selected &amp; profile What can I do to Get More Invitations to Participate? Participant Profile (collection)
=== https://help.respondent.io/en/articles/12552492-screener-explained-how-to-qualify-for-studies ===
What is a screener? A screener is a brief, unpaid questionnaire researchers use to determine if you are a suitable candidate for a paid research study . Learn what screeners are, how they work, tips to qualify for studies , and why you might be disqualified even with a strong profile. Are screeners paid? No. Screeners are not paid. You’re paid only after you attend or complete the study and the researcher confirms your attendance. How screeners work (step-by-step) Find a study in Respondent and click “Start Screener” . Answer the unpaid screener (2–20 questions). The researcher reviews responses and decides whom to invite . If invited, you schedule (for interviews) or complete tasks (for unmoderated). How to pass a screener (do’s &amp; don’ts) Do’s Be honest and specific (job title, tools you actually use, frequency, budgets, timelines). Keep your participant profile updated so answers are consistent. Read carefully for must-have criteria (e.g., region, company size, weekly tool use). Don&#x27;ts Don’t exaggerate or guess. Misrepresentation risks removal from the study/platform. Don’t share sensitive info unless requested on-platform . Double screening scenarios For some projects run with a select group of trusted partners , you may be asked to complete a second screener off-site (on the partner’s platform) after your Respondent screener. What to expect: You’ll complete two screeners : one for the respondent and then one for the partner’s platform . Both screeners are unpaid.
=== https://help.respondent.io/en/articles/12552519-getting-paid-on-respondent-timeline-currencies-how-to-redeem ===
At a glance When you’re paid: After the researcher confirms you attended/completed. How you’re paid: Email from Tremendous → choose a gift card (e.g., VISA prepaid, Amazon, etc.) → redeem. Typical timing: 7–10 business days from confirmation (not the study date). Where to see your payment status Go to your dashboard → Your Projects . Statuses you’ll see: Payment Sent (issued via Tremendous) → Paid (redeemed). How to redeem your incentive When your status shows &#x27; PAID&#x27; , look for an email from Tremendous at your account email address. Open the email and select a gift card of your choice depending on your region (e.g., VISA prepaid, Amazon, Nike, etc.). Follow the redemption instructions by Tremendous. Tip: Can’t find the email? Wait up to 10 business days after getting PAID , then check spam/junk and search for “Tremendous”. When do I get paid? (timeline) Most payments are received within 7–10 business days after the researcher confirms attendance. Business days exclude weekends and public holidays. If the study ended near a holiday/weekend, allow a little extra time. Currencies &amp; payout options Are payments in USD? All incentives are listed and paid in USD . What can I redeem it for? Tremendous shows available payout options by country/region at the time you redeem. Some options may involve currency conversion . If you need a specific method/currency, check the Tremendous email before redeeming. Fees (reminder) Participant incentives are paid minus a fulfillment
